# Retired unsupported CUDA ML lane (Linux x86_64)
#
# This path remains only as a documentation/stub marker for the historical
# `linux-x86_64-cuda` lane. It is intentionally comments-only:
#
# - `core-cuda` in scripts/bootstrap/install_ml_stack.sh fails closed.
# - No checked-in CUDA lockfile is part of the supported requirements contract.
# - Do not install CUDA PyTorch packages ad hoc into the repo `.venv`.
# - Re-establishing CUDA support requires a governed target-owned lock lane.
#
# Historical CUDA lane rationale belongs in governance documentation rather
# than scan-visible pip requirement entries.
